# Environment — VTC Apps

**Naming:** Use **`VTC_*`** env names for platform URLs. Legacy **`POSIF_*`** keys are still injected in parallel during migration — do not commit either in `.env.production`.

## Three layers (do not duplicate)

| Layer | Where | Agent rule |
|-------|--------|------------|
| **Local dev** | `env_development` → copy to `.env.development` (gitignored) | Document every var the app reads; include local values for platform-injected keys |
| **App prod (git)** | `.env.production` — **committed**, not gitignored | **App-owned keys only** — accent, display name, Stripe, app-to-app URLs, map API keys |
| **Platform inject** | build.vtc.com `/opt/generate-app` — **never commit** | `VTC_API_URL`, `DEEPINFRA_*`, realtime/chat/shell URLs — see table below |
| **Build identity** | `apply_app_identity_env_vars` — **never commit** | `APP_NAME`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` — always overwritten |
| **ZAPI per-app** | Dockerfile build step — **never commit** | `MONGODB_URI` |
| **Publish UI** | Developer Environment tab — **not in git** | App secrets (Stripe, custom keys); cannot set reserved/platform keys |

Merge order at deploy (`deployment.mdc`): Developer Environment → platform constants (override repo) → build identity (override name/URL) → `MONGODB_URI` in Docker build.

## Workflow

1. Edit `env_development`; copy to `.env.development` locally
2. Put **only app-owned keys** in `.env.production`; commit and push
3. Never hardcode production URLs in source — landing VTC path cards may use `https://vtc.com` (`landing-page.mdc`)
4. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` / `VITE_` on secrets

